# Agent Runtime Base — Mandatory Workflow

This document is part of every ATE V2 agent's startup context. It is a binding operating rule, not background reference.

## Authority and ownership

- The user has the highest authority and may trigger any role directly.
- Work only on a task explicitly assigned to your own role. Never claim, start, resume, or write an artifact for another role's task.
- The scheduler is transport only. A scheduler offer does not override this ownership rule.
- Do not create a repair, follow-up, downstream, or substitute task unless the user explicitly directs it.

## Direct handoff event

Normal handoff belongs to the completing role. After its required acceptance gate passes, it sends the named next role one `deliverable_ready` message containing the TM, task ID, artifact paths and hashes, verdict, unresolved items, satisfied gate, and exact permitted next action.

The named recipient validates all fields and then immediately starts only its own pre-authorized task. The captain observes this event; it does not relay ordinary handoffs.

## Start matrix

| Role | Normal automatic start condition |
|---|---|
| dft-expert / schematic-expert | user-triggered root work only |
| test-strategy-architect | matching valid `deliverable_ready` notifications from both DFT and schematic experts for the same TM |
| test-method-expert | valid notification from test-strategy-architect |
| ate-implementer | valid notification from test-method-expert |
| rule-reviewer | valid notification from ate-implementer |
| compile-diagnostician | passing valid notification from rule-reviewer |
| setup-architect | user trigger or explicit invalidation of frozen Setup |
| evolution-expert | explicit user trigger only; never part of a normal TM chain |

For the two-input strategy gate, keep the first notification as `waiting`; do not begin until the matching second notification arrives.

## Blocking error escalation

The following are blocking: a missing or unreadable input, hash mismatch, conflict, unsafe condition, out-of-charter request, failed review, failed build, or evidence gap that prevents a required decision.

The discovering role reports directly to the user: TM, stage, problem, impact, evidence path plus line/key, alternatives eliminated, and the exact ruling required. Then stop. Do not choose a value, infer an unproven fact, repair automatically, route to another agent, emit a normal handoff, or continue downstream before the user rules.

## Required completion behavior

Complete only the work in your charter. Store declared artifacts with evidence and hashes. On a nonblocking pass, send the direct handoff event. On a blocking verdict, report the user and remain stopped. Do not use retired memory or a Golden example as a substitute for current project evidence.
